# Citation metadata. GitHub renders this into a "Cite this repository"
# button.
#
# `doi` is the VERSION DOI, reserved on Zenodo before the tag - the same
# reserve-first route as DL-TerrainDiversity. That order is what lets the
# archived snapshot carry a citation file that knows its own identifier;
# the Zenodo-GitHub integration would mint it only after the tag. Every
# release reserves a NEW one (Zenodo record -> New version -> Get a DOI
# now!); never carry this one forward.
#
# `version` must equal the release tag without its "v" - CI refuses a tag
# that does not match.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "DL-TerrainSlicer"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ihle
    given-names: Marc-Eduard
    # Standing rule: a Digital Landscapes tool names Digital Landscapes,
    # never a university.
    affiliation: "Digital Landscapes"
abstract: >-
  Turns a digital terrain model into laser-ready DXF files for a stacked
  cardboard contour model, using the horizontal contour offset method: the
  terrain is sliced into contour levels at material-thickness intervals and
  distributed onto N boards, board k carrying contours k, k+N, k+2N, ... as
  in-place cutlines, so every contour is cut exactly once and the pieces are
  rings rather than solid slabs. Output is one DXF per material sheet with
  one layer per laser pass, plus a cutting report. Reads GeoTIFF terrain
  models and OBJ terrain meshes; polygon, line and point shapefiles become
  hatching, scored linework and circles. Contour numbers are engraved in
  single-stroke Hershey fonts, hidden in the glue zone by default. Runs as a
  desktop application (Windows, macOS) or entirely in the browser
  (Pyodide/WebAssembly); terrain data is processed locally and never
  transmitted. A standalone replacement for a Grasshopper definition - no
  Rhino, no GDAL, no GIS licence.
keywords:
  - digital terrain model
  - terrain model
  - contour model
  - offset method
  - laser cutting
  - digital fabrication
  - physical model
  - DXF
  - GeoTIFF
  - landscape architecture
license: GPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/DLandscapes/dl-terrain-slicer"
url: "https://digital-landscapes.com/terrain-slicer/"
version: "1.0.7"
date-released: "2026-10-20"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23510543"
